### Setup — Product for subscription tests
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: acme

{
  "code": "sub-test-product",
  "name": "Subscription Test Product"
}

### Setup — Plan WITH a trial (14 days)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/plans
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: acme

{
  "productCode": "sub-test-product",
  "code": "sub-trial-monthly",
  "name": "Trial Monthly",
  "intervalUnit": "MONTH",
  "amountCents": 2999,
  "currency": "USD",
  "trialDays": 14
}

### Setup — Plan WITHOUT a trial
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/plans
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: acme

{
  "productCode": "sub-test-product",
  "code": "sub-notrial-monthly",
  "name": "No Trial Monthly",
  "intervalUnit": "MONTH",
  "amountCents": 1999,
  "currency": "USD"
}

### Setup — Customer, capture id for use below
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: acme

{
  "email": "sub-test@acme.test",
  "name": "Subscription Test Customer"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("customerId", response.body.id);
%}


### Create Subscription — WITH trial (expects status TRIALING, currentPeriodEnd ~14 days out)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: acme

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "planCode": "sub-trial-monthly"
}

### Create Subscription — WITHOUT trial (expects status ACTIVE, currentPeriodEnd ~1 month out)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: acme

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "planCode": "sub-notrial-monthly"
}

### Create Subscription — unknown customerId (expects 404 CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: acme

{
  "customerId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "planCode": "sub-trial-monthly"
}

### Create Subscription — unknown planCode (expects 404 PLAN_NOT_FOUND)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: acme

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "planCode": "does-not-exist"
}

### Create Subscription — missing customerId (expects 400 VALIDATION_ERROR)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: acme

{
  "planCode": "sub-trial-monthly"
}

### Create Subscription — missing planCode (expects 400 VALIDATION_ERROR)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: acme

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}"
}

### Create Subscription — tenant isolation check: acme's customerId/planCode used
### under demo tenant (expects 404 CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND — neither the customer
### nor the plan exist for the demo tenant, so this must NOT succeed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: demo

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "planCode": "sub-trial-monthly"
}

### List Subscriptions — all, for acme
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions
X-Tenant-Id: acme

### List Subscriptions — filtered by customerId
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions?customerId={{customerId}}
X-Tenant-Id: acme

### List Subscriptions — tenant isolation check (demo should see none of these)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions
X-Tenant-Id: demo


### Setup — Subscription for state-transition tests (trial plan -> TRIALING)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: acme

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "planCode": "sub-trial-monthly"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("transitionSubId", response.body.id);
%}

### Get Subscription — by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/{{transitionSubId}}
X-Tenant-Id: acme

### Get Subscription — unknown id (expects 404 SUBSCRIPTION_NOT_FOUND)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
X-Tenant-Id: acme

### Get Subscription — tenant isolation: acme's id under demo (expects 404 SUBSCRIPTION_NOT_FOUND)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/{{transitionSubId}}
X-Tenant-Id: demo

### Pause — TRIALING -> PAUSED (expects 200, status PAUSED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/{{transitionSubId}}/pause
X-Tenant-Id: acme

### Pause — already PAUSED (expects 409 INVALID_SUBSCRIPTION_STATE)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/{{transitionSubId}}/pause
X-Tenant-Id: acme

### Resume — PAUSED -> ACTIVE (expects 200, status ACTIVE)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/{{transitionSubId}}/resume
X-Tenant-Id: acme

### Resume — not PAUSED (expects 409 INVALID_SUBSCRIPTION_STATE)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/{{transitionSubId}}/resume
X-Tenant-Id: acme

### Cancel — ACTIVE -> CANCELED (expects 200, status CANCELED, canceledAt set)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/{{transitionSubId}}/cancel
X-Tenant-Id: acme

### Cancel — already CANCELED (expects 409 INVALID_SUBSCRIPTION_STATE)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/{{transitionSubId}}/cancel
X-Tenant-Id: acme

### Pause — a CANCELED subscription (expects 409 INVALID_SUBSCRIPTION_STATE)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/{{transitionSubId}}/pause
X-Tenant-Id: acme

### Cancel — tenant isolation: demo tries to cancel acme's subscription id
### (expects 404 SUBSCRIPTION_NOT_FOUND — must not leak or succeed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/{{transitionSubId}}/cancel
X-Tenant-Id: demo

### Cancel — unknown subscription id (expects 404 SUBSCRIPTION_NOT_FOUND)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/cancel
X-Tenant-Id: acme
